[
    {
        "content": "<p>Yesterday I used <a href=\"https://claude.ai/share/43e316b1-3d66-4a8f-ad48-34f358ae98a2\">Claude</a> together with Aristotle to verify a theorem in untyped λ-calculus:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sn_eta_steps_inv</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Var</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">HasFresh</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Var</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t_st_t'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↠</span><span class=\"n\">η</span><span class=\"bp\">ᶠ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">sn_t'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SN</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FullBeta</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SN</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FullBeta</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">induction</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t_st_t'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">sn_eta_step_inv</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- Natural corollary</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sn_eta_steps_iff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">DecidableEq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Var</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">HasFresh</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Var</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t_st_t'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↠</span><span class=\"n\">η</span><span class=\"bp\">ᶠ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SN</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FullBeta</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SN</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">FullBeta</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">grind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">sn_eta_step</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sn_eta_steps_inv</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The proof is novel — it was invented by Claude. I could not find it in any paper or textbook.</p>\n<p>The key idea is simple: equip the parallel η-reduction (pareta) with a counter. </p>\n<p>The entire process used only free-tier AI.</p>\n<p>Interestingly, one month ago Claude could only produce complicated proofs that were hard to verify and formalize for the same problem.</p>\n<p>Full code:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Claude’s novel contribution (≈300 lines)  <br>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/awesome-lambda-calculus/cslib/blob/sn_eta_step/Cslib/Languages/LambdaCalculus/LocallyNameless/Untyped/ParEtaC.lean\">https://github.com/awesome-lambda-calculus/cslib/blob/sn_eta_step/Cslib/Languages/LambdaCalculus/LocallyNameless/Untyped/ParEtaC.lean</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Final statement  <br>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/awesome-lambda-calculus/cslib/blob/sn_eta_step/Cslib/Languages/LambdaCalculus/LocallyNameless/Untyped/StrongNorm.lean#L190\">https://github.com/awesome-lambda-calculus/cslib/blob/sn_eta_step/Cslib/Languages/LambdaCalculus/LocallyNameless/Untyped/StrongNorm.lean#L190</a></p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
        "id": 612724597,
        "sender_full_name": "lengyijun",
        "timestamp": 1784974694
    },
